@*
    Exception Analysis (migration 257).

    The stage between a raised exception request and the approval
    decision. Reached from Exception Centre's 3-dot menu with
    ?exceptionId=, the way gap-detail is reached from Gap Centre.

    What lives here, and why:

      * The REQUEST DETAIL that used to be captured inside the Approve
        modal. Asking the approver to fill in the requester's case was
        backwards -- the approver's job is to judge it, not to write it.

      * REMEDIATION TASKS. An exception is a decision to accept a gap for
        a time; what is being done about it in the meantime is part of the
        case, not an afterthought. Raise a new task, or map an existing
        one from the exception's practice.

      * SUBMIT FOR APPROVAL, which is the only way a request reaches a
        state where Approve and Reject are offered at all.

    Deliberately NOT here:
      * Linked practice is DISPLAYED, not selected -- it comes from the
        request. A picker here would let the analyst point the exception
        at a different practice than the one that raised it.
      * Linked requirement ref -- dropped.
      * Approval note and compensating control -- the note belongs to the
        approver's form; compensating control is gone.
*@
@model PracticeManagement.Web.Models.PracticeScreen

<div class="pm-page-heading compact">
    <div>
        <p class="pm-eyebrow">@Model.Group / @Model.Title</p>
        <h1 id="exaHeading">Exception Analysis</h1>
        <p id="exaSubHeading">Complete the analysis, attach the remediation work, then submit for approval.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
        @* Bug fix (2026-09-22): this was a bare "/Practice/Index/exception-centre"
           href. That is an absolute path, so it always points at the domain
           root and ignores any PathBase the app is published under (an IIS
           virtual directory / appsettings PathBase) -- worked locally only
           because PathBase is empty there, but 404'd once published under
           one. The fix is the leading "~/": ASP.NET Core's built-in
           UrlResolutionTagHelper (registered app-wide in _ViewImports.cshtml)
           rewrites a "~/"-prefixed href against the request's actual
           PathBase at render time, same as every sibling "Back to..." link
           already does -- see exception-view.cshtml, gap-detail.cshtml,
           gap-view.cshtml and task-view.cshtml's own href="~/Practice/Index/...".
           This was the one place that pattern was missed. *@
        <a class="pm-button" href="~/Practice/Index/exception-centre">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Exception Centre
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="pm-panel" id="exaUnavailable" hidden>
    <div class="pm-empty">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved pm-empty-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <h2 id="exaUnavailableTitle">Exception request not found.</h2>
        <p id="exaUnavailableBody">Open this page from Exception Centre's Actions menu.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="pm-panel" id="exaRoot" hidden>

    @* Read-only context. Everything here is the request as raised --
       nothing on this strip is editable, which is the point. *@
    <div class="pm-toolbar" style="justify-content:space-between">
        <div>
            <span class="pm-badge" id="exaStatusChip">-</span>
            <strong id="exaRequestTitle" style="margin-left:8px"></strong>
        </div>
        <div id="exaSubmitWrap">
            <button class="pm-button primary" id="exaSubmitBtn" type="button">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-paper-plane"></i> Submit for approval
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <dl class="exa-facts" id="exaFacts"></dl>

    <h3 class="exa-section">Analysis</h3>
    <div class="pm-form-grid">
        <label>
            <span>Exception type</span>
            <select id="exaType"><option value="">-- select --</option></select>
        </label>
        <label>
            <span>Exception owner</span>
            <select id="exaOwner"><option value="">-- unassigned --</option></select>
        </label>
        <label class="pm-form-grid-full">
            <span>Justification<span class="pm-required">*</span></span>
            <textarea id="exaJustification" rows="3" maxlength="5000"
                      placeholder="Formal reason the exception is being requested..."></textarea>
        </label>
        <label class="pm-form-grid-full">
            <span>Risk / Impact<span class="pm-required">*</span></span>
            <textarea id="exaRiskImpact" rows="3" maxlength="5000"
                      placeholder="What business/regulatory exposure does this exception carry?"></textarea>
        </label>
        @* Migration 260. The window the analyst is asking for. Required to
           SUBMIT, not to SAVE, so a half-finished analysis can be parked.
           The approver sees these pre-filled and may overrule them; the
           change is recorded in the history below. *@
        <label>
            <span>Effective from<span class="pm-required">*</span></span>
            <input type="date" id="exaEffectiveFrom" />
        </label>
        <label>
            <span>Effective to<span class="pm-required">*</span></span>
            <input type="date" id="exaEffectiveTo" />
        </label>
        <p class="pm-hint pm-form-grid-full">
            The exception window you are requesting. The approver can change it before approving.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="pm-card-actions" style="display:flex; gap:8px; align-items:center; margin:10px 0 4px">
        <button class="pm-button" id="exaSaveBtn" type="button">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-floppy-disk"></i> Save analysis
        </button>
        <span class="pm-form-message" id="exaSaveMsg" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
    </div>

    @* Remediation work. Two routes in, as specified: raise a new task, or
       map one that already exists under this exception's practice. *@
    <h3 class="exa-section">Remediation tasks <span class="pm-badge" id="exaTaskCount">0</span></h3>
    <p class="pm-hint" id="exaTaskHint">
        What is being done about the gap while the exception is in force.
    </p>
    <div class="pm-toolbar">
        <button class="pm-button" id="exaNewTaskBtn" type="button">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i> New task
        </button>
        <button class="pm-button" id="exaMapTaskBtn" type="button">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-link"></i> Map existing task
        </button>
    </div>
    <div class="pm-table-wrap">
        <table id="exaTaskTable">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Task #</th><th>Task</th><th>Type</th>
                    <th>Owner</th><th>Priority</th><th>Due</th>
                    <th>Status</th><th>Link</th><th aria-label="Actions"></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="exaTaskBody">
                <tr><td colspan="9" class="pm-empty">No tasks attached yet.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    @* Migration 260. exception_request_history has been written since 161
       and read by nobody. Traceability that cannot be seen is not
       traceability, so the whole trail is shown here -- including
       EffectiveDatesChanged, which is why this section exists. *@
    <h3 class="exa-section">History</h3>
    <p class="pm-hint">
        Every recorded action on this request, newest first.
    </p>
    <div class="pm-table-wrap">
        <table id="exaHistoryTable">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>When</th><th>Action</th><th>By</th><th>Detail</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="exaHistoryBody">
                <tr><td colspan="4" class="pm-empty">Loading...</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

@* ---------- Map existing task dialog ---------- *@
<div class="pm-modal" id="exaMapModal" hidden>
    <div class="pm-modal-panel pm-modal-wide">
        <header>
            <h2>Map an existing task</h2>
            <button class="pm-modal-close" type="button" data-close-exa-map aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
        </header>
        <div style="padding:0 16px">
            @* Scope note, stated rather than assumed: the picker offers
               the tasks recorded under this exception's practice. *@
            <p class="pm-hint" id="exaMapScope"></p>
            <div class="pm-toolbar">
                <input type="search" id="exaMapSearch" placeholder="Search task title or number..." />
                <button class="pm-button icon" id="exaMapRefresh" type="button" title="Refresh" aria-label="Refresh">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate"></i>
                </button>
            </div>
            @* A checkbox grid, not a row of Map buttons: the ticks ARE
               the link set. Tasks already attached to this exception open
               ticked, so the grid shows the current state rather than
               making the operator remember it. *@
            <div class="pm-table-wrap" style="max-height:50vh; overflow:auto">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th style="width:34px">
                                <input type="checkbox" id="exaMapAll" title="Select all shown" />
                            </th>
                            <th>Task #</th><th>Task</th><th>Type</th>
                            <th>Owner</th><th>Status</th><th>Due</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody id="exaMapBody">
                        <tr><td colspan="7" class="pm-empty">Loading...</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p class="pm-form-message" id="exaMapMsg" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </div>
        <footer class="pm-modal-footer">
            <span class="pm-hint" id="exaMapPending" style="margin-right:auto"></span>
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" data-close-exa-map>Cancel</button>
            <button type="button" class="pm-button primary" id="exaMapSaveBtn">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-floppy-disk"></i> Save
            </button>
        </footer>
    </div>
</div>

@* ---------- New task dialog ----------

   NOT the shared _add-implementation-task-modal partial. That one opens
   window.__openAddImplTask(instanceId, ...) and raises an Implementation
   task against a practice INSTANCE. An exception carries a
   linked_practice_id, not an instance, so reusing it would have created
   the task against an id this page does not have.

   This form posts to the same /practice/api/tasks endpoint Task Centre's
   own "New Task" uses, with the exception's practice as LinkedPracticeId
   and Exception as the source, then links the new task to the request. *@
<div class="pm-modal" id="exaNewTaskModal" hidden>
    <div class="pm-modal-panel">
        <header>
            <h2>New remediation task</h2>
            <button class="pm-modal-close" type="button" data-close-exa-new aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
        </header>
        <form id="exaNewTaskForm">
            <div class="pm-form-grid">
                <label class="pm-form-grid-full">
                    <span>Task name<span class="pm-required">*</span></span>
                    <input type="text" id="exaNtTitle" maxlength="250" required />
                </label>
                <label class="pm-form-grid-full">
                    <span>Description</span>
                    <textarea id="exaNtDescription" rows="3" maxlength="4000"></textarea>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <span>Priority</span>
                    <select id="exaNtPriority">
                        <option value="Low">Low</option>
                        <option value="Medium" selected>Medium</option>
                        <option value="High">High</option>
                        <option value="Critical">Critical</option>
                    </select>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <span>Assign to</span>
                    <select id="exaNtAssignee"><option value="">-- unassigned --</option></select>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <span>Target date</span>
                    <input type="date" id="exaNtTarget" />
                </label>
            </div>
            <p class="pm-form-message" id="exaNtMsg" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
            <footer class="pm-modal-footer">
                <button type="button" class="pm-button" data-close-exa-new>Cancel</button>
                <button type="submit" class="pm-button primary">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i> Create and attach
                </button>
            </footer>
        </form>
    </div>
</div>

<style>
    #exaRoot .exa-section {
        margin: 18px 0 8px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600;
        text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; color: #4a5568;
    }
    #exaRoot .exa-facts {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 240px));
        gap: 8px 20px; margin: 0 0 4px;
    }
    #exaRoot .exa-facts dt {
        font-size: 10px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; color: #758095;
    }
    #exaRoot .exa-facts dd {
        margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 13px; color: #25345a; overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    #exaRoot .pm-hint { font-size: 12px; color: #64748b; margin: 0 0 8px; }
    #exaRoot .pm-required { color: #b91c1c; }
</style>

<script src="~/js/ExceptionCentre/exception-analysis.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
